# Spring Splasher: "Whenever this creature attacks, target creature defending player controls gets -3/-0 until end of turn"
# (CR 508.1m, 603.3, 115.1). Bot2 has two creatures, so the trigger asks which: Bot1's own Ornithopter is refused (not a creature
# the defending player controls), and so is Bot2's Mox Jet - an artifact but not a creature - while Bot2's Ornithopter is the one
# accepted and becomes -3/2 (CR 611.2a). Bot2's Grizzly Bears is untouched: the -3/-0 is applied to the chosen creature alone.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Spring Splasher
Ornithopter
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Emerald
Mox Jet
Grizzly Bears
Ornithopter
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Spring Splasher.Cast
? Bot1.Mana =
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Grizzly Bears.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Attack(Spring Splasher > Bot2)
! Bot1.Target(Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
! Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Jet)
Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.CombatDamage]
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Power = -3

[Expect]
Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Power = -3
Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Toughness = 2
Bot2.Battlefield.Grizzly Bears.Power = 2
Bot2.Battlefield.Grizzly Bears.Toughness = 2
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Power = 0
